ever since the release of layers of fear  in 2016 blueber team's games have been  obsessed with getting you inside the  damaged minds of their characters  sometimes literally  this kind of psychological horror has  become blueber team's calling card and  just this week Konami announced blooper  would be developing the remake of Silent  Hill 2 giving them a chance to bring the  horror classic to a new audience however  their games have also attracted  criticism for their sometimes troubling  messaging around trauma and mental  health so what can we expect from  blooper's reimagination of Silent Hill 2  well whether it's through the Sci-Fi  setting of Observer or the supernatural  mindscapes of the medium one thing is  pretty clear blueber team wants to  create games that get inside your head  too what is the most exciting but what  we are doing is actually that we can  kind of influence the players bring this  feeling to the player that you are not  in control of what is happening around  you  if there's a Common Thread across  blueber team's games it's their emphasis  on the psychological roots of horror  bluebird's games tend to draw influence  from the internal struggles of their  characters to create disturbing and  unsettling horror experiences I spoke to  Mattress Leonard lead director of the  upcoming Silent Hill 2 remake a few  weeks prior to konami's announcement  matches joined blueber team just as they  began work on what would become layers  of fear their first horror game and took  inspiration from films that explore the  dark side of the human psyche movies  like seven cylons of the Lambs The  Shining was something that was a big  inspiration for me as you can see we  don't create like the gore type of games  right so I think those influences that  that me or or making has also are in  line with that right we don't want to  you know create a blood splatter on the  screen is not what we are how we are  working we are mostly creating an  atmosphere and psychological backgrounds  and for the players to be afraid of  though the settings may vary across days  of fear in its sequel Blair Witch  Observer and the medium blooper have  stuck rigidly to this subgenre for the  best part of 10 years with each game  aiming to draw you into the  discomforting psychology of their  protagonists psychological horror is a  sub-genre that you could argue has been  underserved by games since the  flatlining of konami's horror Flagship  so perhaps it's no surprise that blueber  team would pick to remake Silent Hill 2  particularly as the team are so open  about PT's influence on layers of fear  the idea was to play The Haunted House  again and then also like the obvious  influence was speeding from so we saw  that and it was like pretty big thing  back then and we you know we kind of  grab it okay so let's do something like  this after like one week or two weeks we  realized that we don't want to do that  like we want to do something more and  then you know the painter as a  protagonist the overall art background  and that's you know creates the path  that we that we follow laser fear puts  you in the shoes of an unnamed painter  exploring his dilapidated Mansion  functioning is a kind of haunted house  Simulator the player can uncover and  understand more about the character  through finding notes around the  environment hinting at his abusive and  neglectful Behavior towards his wife and  child his fixation on the house is rap  problem and most notably his declining  mental state one note written by a  doctor and apparently annotated by the  painter himself outlines the symptoms of  schizophrenia a commonly misunderstood  condition that does not relate to split  personalities schizophrenia causes among  other things hallucinations and  delusional thinking something that is  represented with worsening severity as  the player progresses a key component of  psychological horror is the idea of the  unreliable narrator the idea that what  the protagonist believes is not  necessarily the objective truth laser  fear allows the player to experience  that firsthand as the painter slips  deeper into psychosis the symptoms of  his condition begin to play out in  increasingly Vivid and unsettling ways  most notably through changes to how he  perceives the environment around him I  think the big game changer for us in the  first layers of fear was actually this  you know this concept of constantly  changing environment around you and it  was something that you know bring this  feeling to the player that you are not  in control of what is happening around  you and we tested for different angles  like whoa like this is something new  like this is something very very cool we  are like very nitpicking about the  environment that we are creating and a  specific character helps a lot because  you know having a painter and many doors  are just open for us how the painter  could see the world the result of this  is a nightmarish trip through a world  that seems to be drawn from the unique  psychological makeup of the protagonist  much as we see throughout the Silent  Hill franchise and particularly with  Silent Hill 2's James Sunderland however  unlike those games layers of fear  features very little of the survival  mechanics you might expect from a  traditional horror game there is no  combat and though you can die at the  hands of the game's monstrous entity the  actual penalty to progression is almost  non-existent this slower Pace extends to  the actual scares too with the balance  weighted towards atmosphere in a steady  increase of tension over constant jump  scares something Bluebird developed  through their later games and that  matches appears Keen to push further in  their upcoming remake the cheapest cares  are distinctious to do most of the time  and you know after creating like you  know several games already in Liberty we  are trying to you know  step back from the jump scares as much  as possible because we realized that  players are scared the most just through  the atmosphere and just their  imagination about what might happen  because the story that you are telling  me is like much stronger than you know  some like cheap jumpscar that will jump  on your face our Inspirations are  changing all the time and something that  might be fitting to the game like layers  of fear might not be fitted to the games  like this like the medium right we had  to have like completely different  approach for that kind of game like I  said like the best part the best story  is when you are connecting everything  every ingredient you are connecting to  the actual topic that you are talking  about this is a trend Blooper have  continued across their back catalog of  games layers of fear 2 Blair Witch  Observer and the medium all center  around horror escapes that are  reflective of the psychological state of  their characters individual traumas  fears secrets and regrets however it's  worth noting that louboutin's depiction  of these psychological conditions  questions and not without controversy  layers of fear essentially suggests the  painter's schizophrenia has turned him  into a monster and some have accused  bluber's most recent game the medium of  promoting damaging stereotypes about  survivors of trauma and abuse in the  media monsters are created in the spirit  world as a result of traumatic events  with the most severe traumas creating  monsters powerful enough to possess  people in the waking World some have  suggested the game's message that you  can't always save everyone paint  survivors of severe trauma as beyond  help an obviously inappropriate and  damaging message to be communicating  when dealing with the kinds of topics  the game addresses similar criticisms  were leveled at another title Blair  Witch the story of which deals with PTSD  and suicide with similarly Bleak  outcomes blueber team are hardly alone  in creating psychological horror art  that attracts controversy however it's  still important to portray these issues  in a considerate way and allow players  to inhabit characters struggling with  their psychological Health in a way that  doesn't stigmatize real-life conditions  and experiences through harmful  stereotypes whatever changes blooper  makes in the Silent Hill 2 remake like  the original they will almost certainly  attempt to put you in the uncomfortable  position of experiencing James's  subjective reality where the horror is  born out of his individual psychological  profile when that kind of psychological  horror is done right it gives the player  a rare opportunity to see through the  eyes of someone at the extreme edge of  their sanity or from the comfort of  their sofa another psychologist or or  anything like this but I think it's  connected with urge to experience  something that you are unable to  experience in your own life this is  something that reached the part of your  mind that you are not using you know  most of the times right this is  something new for your brain for your  you know for your comfortable zones what  was unique for me you know working in a  different companies throughout the years  and start working in Liberty most of the  companies like started from gameplay and  we most most of the time we are starting  from the story for the the premise from  the topic and from from the the  atmosphere and then the game plays  actually like mostly connected to the  story that we are trying to trying to  create we are trying to create  everything based on that  oh so I think this is this is something  that is pretty pretty unique
 

